🐛 Describe the bug
If a python decomposition is registered for an OpOverloadPacket, care must be taken to ensure the decomposition functions for each OpOverload, particularly for operators that have out variants. For example the OpOverloadPacket torch.ops.aten.smooth_l1_loss has an  out overload torch.ops.aten.smooth_l1_loss.out so its python decomposition should support receiving out arguments.
For example callling the below out overload of the smooth_l1_loss op will currently result in error for the Meta dispatch key since its python decomposition does not receive out arguments.
at::_ops::smooth_l1_loss_out::redispatch(self, target, reduction, beta, out);
@register_decomposition(aten.smooth_l1_loss)
@pw_cast_for_opmath
def smooth_l1_loss(..):
    ....
For torch ops that support the out parameter, test_meta_outplace and test_dispatch_meta_outplace cover checking python decompositions still function. However torch ops may not have out parameters but still have out aten overloads that are called e.g. via structured_delegate.
